EXPERIMENT 12 – LOCATING WEB ELEMENTS USING SELENIUM

AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to locate web elements using ID, name, class name, CSS selector and XPath.
ALGORITHM
1. Create a Maven project and add the Selenium 4 dependency.
2. Open the login page of the demo website.
3. Locate the username field using By.id(), password field using By.name() and logo using By.className().
4. Locate the login button using By.cssSelector() and logo using By.xpath().
5. Print the attributes or text of each element.
6. Close the browser.
CODE
Exercise12.java
import org.openqa.selenium.*;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;

public class Exercise12 {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        try {
            driver.manage().window().maximize();
            driver.get("https://www.saucedemo.com");

            WebElement byId =
                driver.findElement(By.id("user-name"));

            WebElement byName =
                driver.findElement(By.name("password"));

            WebElement byClass =
                driver.findElement(By.className("login_logo"));

            WebElement byCss =
                driver.findElement(
                    By.cssSelector("input[type='submit']")
                );

            WebElement byXpath =
                driver.findElement(
                    By.xpath("//div[@class='login_logo']")
                );

            System.out.println("By id : placeholder = "
                + byId.getAttribute("placeholder"));

            System.out.println("By name : placeholder = "
                + byName.getAttribute("placeholder"));

            System.out.println("By className : text = "
                + byClass.getText());

            System.out.println("By cssSelector : value = "
                + byCss.getAttribute("value"));

            System.out.println("By xpath : text = "
                + byXpath.getText());

        } finally {
            driver.quit();
        }
    }
}


INPUT
- Website: https://www.saucedemo.com
- Username field: user-name
- Password field: password
- Logo class: login_logo
OUTPUT
By id          : placeholder = Username
By name        : placeholder = Password
By className   : text = Swag Labs
By cssSelector : value = Login
By xpath       : text = Swag Labs


RESULT
Thus, the Selenium WebDriver program to locate web elements using ID, name, class name, CSS selector and XPath was executed successfully.
